#: processes/activity-log.bpmn:137
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Asked after a task ends: is log capture switched on for this session? `on` persists the entry to the data store. `off or unknown` persists nothing and reports the capture state instead, so an unknown setting is said out loud rather than read as off."
msgstr ""

#: processes/activity-log.bpmn:174
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Asked when a person asks to empty the log: which entries? `one` discards a single entry by id; `all / periodic` discards every entry or a whole session, the branch a scheduled clean-up also takes."
msgstr ""

#: processes/activity-log.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Brackets its own work with a start and an end entry rather than leaving either implied, and reads Gateway_Capture rather than assuming it: persisting when capture is on, but merely reporting the setting — never silently dropping the entry — when it is off or could not be determined."
msgstr ""

#: processes/activity-log.bpmn:136
#. Diagram label
msgid "Capture enabled?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/activity-log.bpmn:144
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Capture is explicitly on — by <folio:log capture=\"on\"/> on the process or by config — so the entries go to the git data store. Only this branch commits anything."
msgstr ""

#: processes/activity-log.bpmn:151
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Capture is off or unknown, so nothing is committed. Say which of the two it is: off is somebody's decision, unknown means nobody could tell, and an agent that believes it has an audit trail when it has none acts on a false belief."
msgstr ""

